# Block / Box

Every component file **opens on `Block`**. `Box` is never a file root.
One file, one `Block`. Nested layout in that file is never `Block`.

`Block` uses `TagGroup.Layout` (`div`, landmarks, `figure`, `search`,
`hgroup`). Omit `tag` only for the application frame: the brick falls back
to `div` and is **not** a landmark. `Box` uses `TagGroup.BoxAllowed` (`div`
only) and exists solely as nested wrap.

## Roots

| Surface | Root | Why |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Application frame (`src/App.svelte`) | `Block` (no `tag`) | viewport `div` |
| Route / view | `Block tag="section"` | page region |
| App chrome header | `Block tag="header"` | banner |
| App chrome main | `Block tag="main"` + `id="main-content"` | primary content |
| Complementary column | `Block tag="aside"` | complementary |

Do not open a file with `Box`, `Stack`, or `Grid`.
Do not put two `Block` roots in one file.
Do not give the application frame `tag="main"` / `section` / `header`.

## Assembly

`header` and `main` are **siblings** inside the frame `Block`. The app frame
opens on that frame and places them next to each other. Do not wrap both in
a third chrome component.

A child **file** may open on its own `Block`. That is composition, not
nested layout.

## Nested

Use `Box`, `Stack`, `Group`, `Grid`, `Nav`, `List`.

- Nested navigation / search → `Nav` (or `List`), never `Block tag="nav"`.
- Centered modal → kit `Dialog`, never `Block` + `role="dialog"`.
- Landmark drawer may keep `Block tag="aside"` with `role="dialog"`.
- CSS grids → `Grid`, not `Box` pretending to be a grid.
- `Box` stays a nested `div`. Never a landmark. Never a file root.

The surface table names the lex-flow Svelte frame. Nested rules stay the same
in any copy of this file.
